/-
# FN-varieties under multiplication and intersection (Kourovka Notebook Problem 2.43)

Kourovka Notebook, Archive of Solved Problems, Problem 2.43 (A. I. Mal'cev): a group `G` is an
FN-group if the groups `γᵢG/γᵢ₊₁G` are free abelian and `⋂ᵢ γᵢG = 1`; a variety is a Σ-variety if
its free groups have the property Σ. (a) Which properties Σ are preserved under multiplication and
intersection of varieties? Is the FN property preserved under these operations? (b) Are all
varieties obtained by multiplication and intersection from the nilpotent varieties `𝔑₁, 𝔑₂, …`
FN-varieties?
-/

module

public import Batteries.Util.ProofWanted
public import Mathlib.GroupTheory.FreeAbelianGroup
public import Mathlib.GroupTheory.Nilpotent

@[expose] public section

namespace MathlibExt.GroupTheory.FNVarietiesProductIntersectionKourovka2Problem43Wanted

/-!
Source: E. I. Khukhro and V. D. Mazurov (eds.), Unsolved Problems in Group Theory: The Kourovka
Notebook, 21st issue, arXiv:1401.0300v49 (2026), Archive of Solved Problems, Problem 2.43 (A. I.
Mal'cev). UnsolvedMath record UM-00700116 (`KOU-2.43`), dataset ulamai/UnsolvedMath v1.8.0.

A variety is given by a set of laws `L ⊆ FreeGroup ℕ`; its free group of rank `n` is `FreeGroup (Fin
n)` modulo the verbal subgroup generated by the values of the words of `L`, and an FN-variety is one
whose free groups of every finite rank are FN-groups (FN for all finite ranks implies FN for
countable rank, since lower central factors of the countable-rank free group are unions of chains of
direct summands). The product `𝔘𝔙` has the laws `𝔘(𝔙(F))` of `F = FreeGroup ℕ`, the intersection has
the union of the law sets, and `𝔑_c` is defined by `[x₀, …, x_c] = 1`. The open-ended first question
of (a), which properties are preserved, is not formalized.
-/

/-- The verbal subgroup of `G` for the set of laws `L ⊆ FreeGroup ℕ`: the (normal) subgroup
generated by all values `w(g₀, g₁, …)` of words `w ∈ L` in `G`. -/
abbrev verbalSubgroup (L : Set (FreeGroup ℕ)) (G : Type) [Group G] : Subgroup G :=
  Subgroup.normalClosure {x | ∃ w ∈ L, ∃ g : ℕ → G, x = FreeGroup.lift g w}

/-- The free group of rank `n` of the variety defined by the laws `L`. -/
abbrev RelativelyFreeGroup (L : Set (FreeGroup ℕ)) (n : ℕ) : Type :=
  FreeGroup (Fin n) ⧸ verbalSubgroup L (FreeGroup (Fin n))

/-- A group is free abelian: multiplicatively isomorphic to a free abelian group. -/
def IsFreeAbelianGroup (Q : Type) [Group Q] : Prop :=
  ∃ X : Type, Nonempty (Q ≃* Multiplicative (FreeAbelianGroup X))

/-- `G` is an `FN`-group: the factors `γᵢ G / γᵢ₊₁ G` of the lower central series are free abelian
and `⋂ᵢ γᵢ G = 1` (`(⊤ : Subgroup G).lowerCentralSeries i` is `γᵢ₊₁ G`). -/
def IsFNGroup (G : Type) [Group G] : Prop :=
  (∀ i : ℕ, IsFreeAbelianGroup ((⊤ : Subgroup G).lowerCentralSeries i ⧸
    ((⊤ : Subgroup G).lowerCentralSeries (i + 1)).subgroupOf
      ((⊤ : Subgroup G).lowerCentralSeries i))) ∧
    ⨅ i, (⊤ : Subgroup G).lowerCentralSeries i = ⊥

/-- The variety defined by `L` is an `FN`-variety: all its relatively free groups (of every finite
rank) are `FN`-groups. -/
def IsFNVariety (L : Set (FreeGroup ℕ)) : Prop :=
  ∀ n : ℕ, IsFNGroup (RelativelyFreeGroup L n)

/-- Laws of the product variety `𝔘𝔙` (groups with a normal `𝔘`-subgroup and `𝔙`-quotient): the
`𝔘`-verbal subgroup of the `𝔙`-verbal subgroup of `FreeGroup ℕ`. -/
def productLaws (LU LV : Set (FreeGroup ℕ)) : Set (FreeGroup ℕ) :=
  ((verbalSubgroup LU (verbalSubgroup LV (FreeGroup ℕ))).map
    (verbalSubgroup LV (FreeGroup ℕ)).subtype : Set (FreeGroup ℕ))

/-- The left-normed commutator `[x₀, x₁, …, x_c]`, with `[a, b] = a b a⁻¹ b⁻¹`. -/
def leftNormedCommutator : ℕ → FreeGroup ℕ
  | 0 => FreeGroup.of 0
  | c + 1 => leftNormedCommutator c * FreeGroup.of (c + 1) * (leftNormedCommutator c)⁻¹ *
      (FreeGroup.of (c + 1))⁻¹

/-- Law sets of the varieties obtained from the nilpotent varieties `𝔑_c`, `c ≥ 1` (defined by
`[x₀, …, x_c] = 1`), by multiplication and intersection (the union of law sets). -/
inductive IsGeneratedFromNilpotentVarieties : Set (FreeGroup ℕ) → Prop
  | nilpotent (c : ℕ) (hc : 1 ≤ c) : IsGeneratedFromNilpotentVarieties {leftNormedCommutator c}
  | product {LU LV : Set (FreeGroup ℕ)} : IsGeneratedFromNilpotentVarieties LU →
      IsGeneratedFromNilpotentVarieties LV → IsGeneratedFromNilpotentVarieties (productLaws LU LV)
  | intersection {LU LV : Set (FreeGroup ℕ)} : IsGeneratedFromNilpotentVarieties LU →
      IsGeneratedFromNilpotentVarieties LV → IsGeneratedFromNilpotentVarieties (LU ∪ LV)

/-- Kourovka 2.43(a) (A. I. Mal'cev), multiplication: the product of two `FN`-varieties is an
`FN`-variety. -/
def fnVarietiesClosedUnderProduct : Prop :=
  ∀ LU LV : Set (FreeGroup ℕ), IsFNVariety LU → IsFNVariety LV → IsFNVariety (productLaws LU LV)

/-- Kourovka 2.43(a), intersection: the intersection of two `FN`-varieties is an `FN`-variety. -/
def fnVarietiesClosedUnderIntersection : Prop :=
  ∀ LU LV : Set (FreeGroup ℕ), IsFNVariety LU → IsFNVariety LV → IsFNVariety (LU ∪ LV)

/-- Kourovka 2.43(b): every variety obtained from `𝔑₁, 𝔑₂, …` by multiplication and intersection
is an `FN`-variety. -/
def nilpotentGeneratedVarietiesAreFN : Prop :=
  ∀ L : Set (FreeGroup ℕ), IsGeneratedFromNilpotentVarieties L → IsFNVariety L

/--
Resolved true: the Kourovka Archive records that the FN property is preserved by multiplication of
varieties (Shmel'kin, 1973). Source: E. I. Khukhro and V. D. Mazurov (eds.), Unsolved Problems in
Group Theory: The Kourovka Notebook, 21st issue, arXiv:1401.0300v49 (2026), Archive of Solved
Problems, Problem 2.43 (A. I. Mal'cev); resolution: A. L. Shmel'kin, Trans. Moscow Math. Soc. 29
(1973), 239-252; L. G. Kovács, example in A. N. Krasil'nikov, letter of 17 July 1998 (using P.
Fitzpatrick and L. G. Kovács, J. Austral. Math. Soc. Ser. A 35 (1983), 59-73); Yu. M. Gorchakov,
Algebra i Logika 6 (1967), no. 3, 25-30, Kourovka Archive, Problem 2.43: a) FN is preserved by
multiplication (Shmel'kin) and not by intersection (Kovács: the class-4 varieties U, V defined by
[x,y,y,x] = 1 and [[x,y],[z,t]] = 1 are FN, but the rank-3 free group of U ∩ V is not torsion-free);
b) Yes (Gorchakov), https://arxiv.org/abs/1401.0300v49.
-/
public theorem_wanted fnVarietiesClosedUnderProduct_holds : fnVarietiesClosedUnderProduct

/--
Resolved false: the Kourovka Archive records L. G. Kovács's example (communicated by A. N.
Krasil'nikov, 1998): the varieties `𝔘` and `𝔙` of nilpotent groups of class at most `4` satisfying
`[x, y, y, x] = 1`, respectively `[[x, y], [z, t]] = 1`, are FN-varieties, but the free group of
rank `3` of `𝔘 ∩ 𝔙` is not torsion-free, so `𝔘 ∩ 𝔙` is not an FN-variety. Source: E. I. Khukhro and
V. D. Mazurov (eds.), Unsolved Problems in Group Theory: The Kourovka Notebook, 21st issue,
arXiv:1401.0300v49 (2026), Archive of Solved Problems, Problem 2.43 (A. I. Mal'cev); resolution: A.
L. Shmel'kin, Trans. Moscow Math. Soc. 29 (1973), 239-252; L. G. Kovács, example in A. N.
Krasil'nikov, letter of 17 July 1998 (using P. Fitzpatrick and L. G. Kovács, J. Austral. Math. Soc.
Ser. A 35 (1983), 59-73); Yu. M. Gorchakov, Algebra i Logika 6 (1967), no. 3, 25-30, Kourovka
Archive, Problem 2.43: a) FN is preserved by multiplication (Shmel'kin) and not by intersection
(Kovács: the class-4 varieties U, V defined by [x,y,y,x] = 1 and [[x,y],[z,t]] = 1 are FN, but the
rank-3 free group of U ∩ V is not torsion-free); b) Yes (Gorchakov),
https://arxiv.org/abs/1401.0300v49.
-/
public theorem_wanted fnVarietiesClosedUnderIntersection_refuted :
    ¬ fnVarietiesClosedUnderIntersection

/--
Resolved true: the Kourovka Archive answers 2.43(b) "Yes" (Gorchakov, 1967): every variety obtained
from `𝔑₁, 𝔑₂, …` by multiplication and intersection is an FN-variety. Source: E. I. Khukhro and V.
D. Mazurov (eds.), Unsolved Problems in Group Theory: The Kourovka Notebook, 21st issue,
arXiv:1401.0300v49 (2026), Archive of Solved Problems, Problem 2.43 (A. I. Mal'cev); resolution: A.
L. Shmel'kin, Trans. Moscow Math. Soc. 29 (1973), 239-252; L. G. Kovács, example in A. N.
Krasil'nikov, letter of 17 July 1998 (using P. Fitzpatrick and L. G. Kovács, J. Austral. Math. Soc.
Ser. A 35 (1983), 59-73); Yu. M. Gorchakov, Algebra i Logika 6 (1967), no. 3, 25-30, Kourovka
Archive, Problem 2.43: a) FN is preserved by multiplication (Shmel'kin) and not by intersection
(Kovács: the class-4 varieties U, V defined by [x,y,y,x] = 1 and [[x,y],[z,t]] = 1 are FN, but the
rank-3 free group of U ∩ V is not torsion-free); b) Yes (Gorchakov),
https://arxiv.org/abs/1401.0300v49.
-/
public theorem_wanted nilpotentGeneratedVarietiesAreFN_holds : nilpotentGeneratedVarietiesAreFN

end MathlibExt.GroupTheory.FNVarietiesProductIntersectionKourovka2Problem43Wanted
